// P3G.4 (derived-and-linking.md DV3.2–DV3.8, DV1.5; ex-dv1's values): the Derived feature's
// options. A "Block source" (the 50 × 30 × 25 block, part number BLK-001; "Sketch 2" a 20 × 10
// rectangle at (0, 40)–(20, 50); "Mate connector 1" at the top-face centre (25, 15, 25), on the
// block; V1) and B "Block derived" ("Part Studio 1" with "Mate connector 1" at (0, 0, 100);
// "Plate") (`derived setup`); Derived 1 from A@V1 at the origin and at Mate connector 1
// (`derived dv1`, ex-dv1).
// 01 (ex-dv1) two copies, "Part 1" and "Part 1 (2)": V = 2 · 37 500 = 75 000 mm³, area 14 000,
//    centroid (25, 15, 62.5).
// 02 Derived 1 reopened (double-click): Locations "Origin", "Mate connector 1".
// 03 "Origin" removed: one copy, on Mate connector 1 (the source's origin onto it: z 100..125).
// 04 Placement → Base mate connector: the source's "Mate connector 1" is the base; its top-face
//    centre goes onto (0, 0, 100), so the block sits under it (z 75..100).
// 05 Include mate connectors ticked: the derived connector comes along, its triad drawn at
//    (0, 0, 100) on the block's top face (over the coplanar face, as the host's).
// 06 ✓, the block's mass: V 37 500, centroid (0, 0, 87.5).
// 07 a Ø10 hole cut through the derived block (`derived hole`): 37 500 − π·5²·25 = 35 536.505.
// 08 Derived 1 reopened: Part Studio unticked, Part 1, Sketch 2 and Plane 1 ticked; the derived
//    sketch shows placed (z 75, x −25..−5, y −35..−25) and the derived Plane 1 is drawn with its
//    label (z 115); the derived connector's triad shows on the block's top face.
// 09 the derived Sketch 2 extruded 5 (`derived extrude-sketch`): "Part 2" (Aluminum - 6061),
//    20·10·5 = 1 000 mm³, 2.700 g.
// 09b (P3G.5) Extrude 2 reopened: its field's item "Face of Sketch 2 (Derived 1)" (cut to fit,
//    whole in its tooltip).
// 10 Derived 1's children: Part 1 (eye), Sketch 2 (used by the extrude, so hidden), Plane 1, Mate
//    connector 1.
// 11 the derived Plane 1's row hovered: its eye.
// 12 the eye clicked: the derived plane is hidden (its row greyed).
// 13 Include properties on: Part 1's Properties show the source's part number BLK-001.
// 14 Include properties off (reopened, unticked, ✓): the part number is gone; the name and the
//    material (Aluminum - 6061) stay.
// 15 (DV1.5) Plate derives Part Studio 1 at the workspace (`derived plate-derives-host`); in
//    Part Studio 1, Insert → Current document → Plate is refused: "Circular reference: Block
//    derived › Part Studio 1 → Block derived › Plate → Block derived".
// 16 ✕ (the refusal's toast goes with the dialog), then the Plate tab: its Derived 1 follows Part
//    Studio 1 (the block with its hole, Part 2) beside the plate: before.
// 17 back in Part Studio 1, the hole's Extrude 1 → Suppress.
// 18 the Plate tab again: its derived block has no hole now (live, no update): after.
